01:15:31.660 --> 01:15:34.101
Was that the idea?
- Yeah, yeah.

01:15:34.101 --> 01:15:35.302
I think that's about it.
- Oh, okay.

01:15:35.302 --> 01:15:37.220
I mean I feel like I missed a key word.

01:15:37.220 --> 01:15:38.135
But, that's, okay--

01:15:38.135 --> 01:15:39.053
- Yeah, that's what it is.
- That's the gist

01:15:39.053 --> 01:15:39.886
of the question?
- Yeah.

01:15:39.886 --> 01:15:43.200
- Well yeah, I mean they sort of represent

01:15:43.200 --> 01:15:44.940
two styles of thinking, right?

01:15:44.940 --> 01:15:47.540
That algebra has this virtue
of being very systematic,

01:15:47.540 --> 01:15:49.210
you can, as I said earlier you

01:15:49.210 --> 01:15:51.940
could massage equations,
manipulate symbols.

01:15:51.940 --> 01:15:53.203
You in a way don't have to think.

01:15:53.203 --> 01:15:55.410
Like you don't have to
have insight to do algebra.

01:15:55.410 --> 01:15:57.940
You just have to do the
bookkeeping correctly,

01:15:57.940 --> 01:15:59.280
and that's one of the great strengths.

01:15:59.280 --> 01:16:01.973
Actually, Leibniz when
he's doing calculus,

01:16:02.870 --> 01:16:06.180
his version of calculus says and actually

01:16:06.180 --> 01:16:07.970
he's the one who gives
us the world calculus.

01:16:07.970 --> 01:16:11.280
He says you know, what
the virtue of my calculus,

01:16:11.280 --> 01:16:14.580
at first he calls it my
calculus, my way of thinking,

01:16:14.580 --> 01:16:16.330
my style of reasoning.

01:16:16.330 --> 01:16:18.270
Newton doesn't refer to
it as calculus by the way.

01:16:18.270 --> 01:16:19.690
He calls it fluxions.

01:16:19.690 --> 01:16:21.890
He's interested in the world in flux.

01:16:21.890 --> 01:16:25.390
So but anyway, so Leibniz
says something like

01:16:25.390 --> 01:16:28.760
the virtue of my calculus
is that it frees the mind,

01:16:28.760 --> 01:16:30.550
frees the imagination.

01:16:30.550 --> 01:16:32.510
You don't have to spend
any effort thinking,

01:16:32.510 --> 01:16:34.040
you're just, it's like knitting.

01:16:34.040 --> 01:16:36.500
You know, you just move the
symbols around, it's all good.

01:16:36.500 --> 01:16:39.730
Whereas geometry, although
it's extremely intuitive

01:16:39.730 --> 01:16:44.210
and visual, requires tremendous
ingenuity and you know,

01:16:44.210 --> 01:16:47.870
this is partly why it takes
2,000 years after Archimedes for

01:16:47.870 --> 01:16:51.490
anyone to really advance
calculus much beyond what he did,

01:16:51.490 --> 01:16:54.920
because he was such a
towering genius that,

01:16:54.920 --> 01:16:58.000
and there were no tools for
everyone else, you know?

01:16:58.000 --> 01:16:59.840
I mean if you couldn't
reason like Archimedes

01:16:59.840 --> 01:17:03.340
geometrically or invent,
I'm exaggerating because

01:17:03.340 --> 01:17:05.280
there were things that
were done after him,

01:17:05.280 --> 01:17:09.230
but progress was very slow
