01:25:37.060 --> 01:25:38.560
in most conceptions in God--

01:25:38.560 --> 01:25:40.490
- Then anything measurable.
- Then of course.

01:25:40.490 --> 01:25:41.860
- Could be like.
- Yeah, well a couple

01:25:41.860 --> 01:25:45.590
of big if statements there.
- Yeah.

01:25:45.590 --> 01:25:47.984
- Yeah, I don't know.

01:25:47.984 --> 01:25:51.170
I don't know, I don't,
okay so the word God gets

01:25:51.170 --> 01:25:52.710
used a lot in different ways, right?

01:25:52.710 --> 01:25:55.610
Einstein talks about God,
but he was careful to say

01:25:55.610 --> 01:25:59.610
not the God who cares about you know,

01:25:59.610 --> 01:26:01.200
whether you've been naughty or nice.

01:26:01.200 --> 01:26:03.630
It's the God, the creator
of the universe God,

01:26:03.630 --> 01:26:06.180
who makes the laws of nature, et cetera.

01:26:06.180 --> 01:26:07.970
Or maybe just the laws themself.

01:26:07.970 --> 01:26:11.110
Like he always used to say, I'm
talking about Spinoza's God.

01:26:11.110 --> 01:26:14.270
Meaning the God that is nature,

01:26:14.270 --> 01:26:16.540
not the God, not a personal
God who cares about

01:26:16.540 --> 01:26:18.160
sin and things like that.

01:26:18.160 --> 01:26:21.450
So that, if we just mean nature.

01:26:21.450 --> 01:26:22.820
I mean it's still a big mystery.

01:26:22.820 --> 01:26:25.420
I do feel this is a mystery that's running

01:26:25.420 --> 01:26:28.130
throughout the story as I tell it.

01:26:28.130 --> 01:26:30.840
That why can math, I do actually,

01:26:30.840 --> 01:26:32.440
I didn't really raise
this question clearly.

01:26:32.440 --> 01:26:33.650
Let me try to raise it now.

01:26:33.650 --> 01:26:35.780
Why does math work?

01:26:35.780 --> 01:26:38.310
In, yeah okay, let's
suppose we restrict ourself

01:26:38.310 --> 01:26:39.810
to the domain you're talking about.

01:26:39.810 --> 01:26:41.800
The domain of things that can be measured.

01:26:41.800 --> 01:26:46.130
It's still a question, why
does nature obey logic?

01:26:46.130 --> 01:26:48.050
In particular, human logic.

01:26:48.050 --> 01:26:51.310
That's, it's not obvious to me
that that should be possible.

01:26:51.310 --> 01:26:53.820
We're not the best thing imaginable.

01:26:53.820 --> 01:26:57.030
We're you know, a few generations
removed from primates,

01:26:57.030 --> 01:27:02.030
and we have logic that can
get the gyromagnetic ratio

01:27:02.610 --> 01:27:04.810
of the electron to eight digits.

01:27:04.810 --> 01:27:09.540
That's weird that our puny logic matches

01:27:09.540 --> 01:27:12.120
what really goes on in
this universe this well.

01:27:12.120 --> 01:27:14.330
It didn't, I don't know why that worked.

01:27:14.330 --> 01:27:15.163
Why does it work?

01:27:15.163 --> 01:27:17.900
This is the question that
Eugene Wigner famously asked.

01:27:17.900 --> 01:27:21.040
You know, of the unreasonable
effectiveness of mathematics.

01:27:21.040 --> 01:27:24.610
And lots of people have
wondered about this.

01:27:24.610 --> 01:27:27.760
Some would say it's because God
made the world very orderly.

01:27:27.760 --> 01:27:30.730
Others say, if the world
were very disorderly,

01:27:30.730 --> 01:27:32.750
we would not be able to evolve

01:27:32.750 --> 01:27:34.960
to even our puny level of intelligence.

01:27:34.960 --> 01:27:38.390
Like only universes that
support enough order

01:27:38.390 --> 01:27:41.300
to allow intelligent life,
those are the only universes

01:27:41.300 --> 01:27:42.560
we can observe.

01:27:42.560 --> 01:27:45.000
So it's sort of, that's the anthropic view

01:27:45.000 --> 01:27:46.880
of why the universe makes sense.

01:27:46.880 --> 01:27:47.830
(muffed talking)
Yes.

01:27:47.830 --> 01:27:49.640
